Third-party material

vendor/opencascade and vendor/opencascade-sys are the opencascade and opencascade-sys 0.3.0
crates by Brian Schwind (https://github.com/bschwind/opencascade-rs), built only by
camcraft-import's `opencascade` feature, for cross-checking. They are licensed under
the GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1, not under camcraft's licences, and their licence is
in vendor/opencascade/LICENSE and vendor/opencascade-sys/LICENSE. camcraft modifies them: fixes
so they build and link with MSVC, and each B-rep face's triangle count, which picking needs.
Diffing either crate against the published 0.3.0 shows every change.

Through the occt-sys crate they build Open CASCADE Technology (https://dev.opencascade.org)
from source and link it statically. It is licensed under the LGPL 2.1 with the Open CASCADE
exception. A build without that feature contains none of it; see the README's License section
and docs/decisions/0001-step-backend.md.

STEP import is ogeom (https://github.com/gilbertorconde/ogeom-rs), MIT or Apache-2.0.

The app's fonts are IBM Plex Sans and Fira Code, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, and a
subset of Lucide's icons, under the ISC licence. crates/camcraft-gui/assets/fonts/ holds each
licence and where each file came from.

